			<div class="content" id="post-content-1763654">
									

<p>So, the last note implies that the GOC think they have them all, and will try to destroy them simultaneously, at which point those that are contained by the Foundation will go boom. Am I getting this right? Why can't this be solved by just warning GOC, seeing as it's one of the few groups the Foundation is on speaking terms with?</p>
<p>Also, apart from some awkward sentence structure, the designation is confusing, referring both to the buckets and to the entities that come out from the buckets.</p>
<p>Also also, the connection to the fallout shelters isn't really clear. I expected the entities to tear people apart so that they can reassemble them after the war is over and the radiation levels are low enough, with hook being in the imperfections of the reassembling process; but this isn't hinted at all in the article, so it's likely this wasn't author's intention. Which leaves me puzzled about the shelters.</p>
<p>I don't know, I like bits of this. I'll no-vote for now, but I might revote later.</p>

