<blockquote>
<p>My mental picture had them under some giant hydraulic piston in some reinforced chamber somewhere. A &quot;boot&quot; for the can seems it would be insufficient for anticipated future breaches.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>But that's kinda the problem. The containment procedures don't actually specify how is it contained - saying &quot;held down by 14&#160;MPa&quot;, is vague and meaningless from the perspective of what's being done, nevermind that a value with an unit without defining what is it a measure of is horrid tone.<br />
Nevermind that encasing it tightly would work better, and the fact that the internal pressure (if it's 14MPa) is already enough to go over yield stress of aluminium - I'm just taking that they're fancy anomalous barrels made of something excessively strong.</p>

